60,3,1,talk,Kenji,,Anchor Industrial Software seems best for our yards. They are built for transport and stay during rollout.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, but the subscription model of Tessera might be cheaper long-term. The invoices showed bundled deals are stable.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, Tessera uses a partner for migration. That is risky. We need direct ownership.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, I agree. The 2018 data lift was done by an external team and failed. We need a vendor who handles it themselves.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Servas,,"@All, Anchor's engineering team staying through rollout addresses my concern about the retiring admins.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Servas, yes, and they are on our own servers. That means we control the upgrades.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, but on-premise means we pay for maintenance separately. The invoices showed that costs climb.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, true, but the support ownership is clear. No more scattered suppliers.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, I am still worried about the data migration. Anchor is on-premise, so they need to handle the lift carefully.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Rin, their team is present. That is a good sign. The supervisors might respect them more.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@All, I am voting for Anchor. It fits our yard needs and the rollout plan.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Kenji, I am hesitant. The long-term cost is unclear. But the bundled price of Tessera is tempting.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Mizuki, I am voting for Anchor. The clear ownership and on-premise control are worth the cost.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Rin,,"@Asuka, I am voting for Anchor. The presence of their team during rollout is crucial for the data lift.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Servas,,"@All, I am voting for Anchor. The human factor is addressed. The team stays with us.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
